 "c0af9db6-5918-5172-a76f-e795c725976c" 13194139535067 true] [17592186329501 1145 "Recall that every quadratic form defined on ${R}^{4}$ has an associated $4\\times 4$ symmetric matrix.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- $D$ *cannot* be a matrix of a quadratic form defined on ${R}^{4}.$ Although it's a $4\\times 4$ matrix, $D$ is not symmetric since ${d}_{24}\\ne {d}_{42}.$\n\n- $E$ *cannot* be a matrix of a quadratic form defined on ${R}^{4}$ since it's a $2\\times 2$ matrix (not $4\\times 4$).\n\n- $F$ could be a matrix of a quadratic form defined on ${R}^{4}$ since it is a $4\\times 4$ symmetric matrix.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$F$ only.\"" 13194139535067 true] [17592186329502 1000 #edb/ref 17592186329503 13194139535067 true] [17592186329502 1000 #edb/ref 17592186329504 13194139535067 true] [17592186329502 1000 #edb/ref 17592186329505 13194139535067 true] [17592186329502 1000 #edb/ref 17592186329506 13194139535067 true] [17592186329502 1000 #edb/ref 17592186329507 13194139535067 true] [17592186329502 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535067 true] [17592186329502 1041 "selection" 13194139535067 true] [17592186329502 1104 #edb/ref 17592186329505 13194139535067 true] [17592186329502 1110 #uuid "5442bd65-48e9-5ebd-a85f-3791b0368e54" 13194139535067 true] [17592186329503 1034 "$D$ only" 13194139535067 true] [17592186329503 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535067 true] [17592186329503 1111 #uuid "81e75160-4372-5a2e-862c-540c97f229a7" 13194139535067 true] [17592186329504 1034 "$D$ and $F$ only" 13194139535067 true] [17592186329504 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535067 true] [17592186329504 1111 #uuid "259e4baa-b429-5e75-9ff2-0e9c00f26ba6" 13194139535067 true] [17592186329505 1034 "$F$ only" 13194139535067 true] [17592186329505 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535067 true] [17592186329505 1111 #uuid "c557f540-6a99-56b2-93fc-ef96b910ee2a" 13194139535067 true] [17592186329506 1034 "$E$ only" 13194139535067 true] [1759